Deliberately empty.

Firebase Hosting requires a static directory, and this one exists so that it
finds nothing: every request falls through to the rewrite in firebase.json and
is served by Cloud Run.

It is NOT Next.js's public/ directory. Pointing Firebase at that one would
publish those assets to the edge, where they would be served by Hosting instead
of the application and would not change when the container is redeployed. Do not
repoint this at public/.
